{"parse":{"title":"119th United States Congress","pageid":70645797,"text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Senate_membership_changes\">Senate membership changes</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=119th_United_States_Congress&amp;veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Senate membership changes\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-divider\"> | </span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=119th_United_States_Congress&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section&#039;s source code: Senate membership changes\"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1368532237\">.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_special_elections_to_the_United_States_Senate\" title=\"List of special elections to the United States Senate\">List of special elections to the United States Senate</a></div>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n\n<caption>Senate changes\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr style=\"vertical-align:bottom;\">\n<th scope=\"col\">State<br />(class)\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Vacated by\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" data-sort-type=\"date\">Reason for change\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Successor\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" data-sort-type=\"date\"><span class=\"nowrap\">Date of successor's</span><br /><span class=\"nowrap\">formal installation<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SuccessorInstallation&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SuccessorInstallation-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>a<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_West_Virginia\" title=\"List of United States senators from West Virginia\">West&#160;Virginia</a><br />(1)\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Aaaaa\">Vacant\n</td>\n<td>Senator-elect chose to wait until finishing his term as <a href=\"/wiki/Governor_of_West_Virginia\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Governor of West Virginia\">Governor of West Virginia</a> before taking his seat.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Justice, Jim\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Jim_Justice\" title=\"Jim Justice\">Jim Justice</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>January 14, 2025\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Ohio\" title=\"List of United States senators from Ohio\">Ohio</a><br />(3)\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Vance, JD\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/JD_Vance\" title=\"JD Vance\">JD Vance</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned January 10, 2025, to become <a href=\"/wiki/Vice_President_of_the_United_States\" title=\"Vice President of the United States\">Vice President of the United States</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />Successor was appointed January 18, 2025, to continue the term.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Husted, Jon\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Jon_Husted\" title=\"Jon Husted\">Jon Husted</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>January 21, 2025<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Weaver&#95;6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Weaver-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Florida\" title=\"List of United States senators from Florida\">Florida</a><br />(3)\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Rubio, Marco\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Marco_Rubio\" title=\"Marco Rubio\">Marco Rubio</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned January 20, 2025, to become <a href=\"/wiki/United_States_Secretary_of_State\" title=\"United States Secretary of State\">United States Secretary of State</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />Successor was appointed January 21, 2025, to continue the term.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />Appointee was later <a href=\"/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_special_election_in_Florida\" title=\"2026 United States Senate special election in Florida\">elected</a> to finish the term ending January 3, 2029.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Moody, Ashley\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ashley_Moody\" title=\"Ashley Moody\">Ashley Moody</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>January 21, 2025<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Weaver&#95;6-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Weaver-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Oklahoma\" title=\"List of United States senators from Oklahoma\">Oklahoma</a><br />(2)\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span class=\"nowrap\"><span data-sort-value=\"Mullin, Markwayne\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Markwayne_Mullin\" title=\"Markwayne Mullin\">Markwayne Mullin</a></span></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent resigned March 23, 2026, to become <a href=\"/wiki/United_States_Secretary_of_Homeland_Security\" title=\"United States Secretary of Homeland Security\">United States Secretary of Homeland Security</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-9\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />Successor was appointed to finish the term.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Armstrong, Alan\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Alan_Armstrong\" title=\"Alan Armstrong\">Alan Armstrong</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>March 24, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_South_Carolina\" title=\"List of United States senators from South Carolina\">South Carolina</a><br />(2)\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Graham, Lindsey\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lindsey_Graham\" title=\"Lindsey Graham\">Lindsey Graham</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Incumbent died July 11, 2026.<br />Successor was <a href=\"/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_South_Carolina#Interim_appointment\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in South Carolina\">appointed</a> July 14, 2026, to finish the term.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Graham, Darline\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Darline_Graham\" title=\"Darline Graham\">Darline Graham</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>July 14, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Oklahoma\" title=\"List of United States senators from Oklahoma\">Oklahoma</a><br />(2)\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Armstrong, Alan\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Alan_Armstrong\" title=\"Alan Armstrong\">Alan Armstrong</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>Appointee resigning early following state law determination.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Hern&#95;10-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Hern-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />Successor will be appointed November 30, 2026, having already been <a href=\"/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_Oklahoma\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in Oklahoma\">elected</a> to the next term.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Hern, Kevin\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Kevin_Hern\" title=\"Kevin Hern\">Kevin Hern</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td>November 30, 2026\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Ohio\" title=\"List of United States senators from Ohio\">Ohio</a><br />(3)\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"Husted, Jon\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Jon_Husted\" title=\"Jon Husted\">Jon Husted</a></span></span></span><br />(R)\n</td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"TBD 2026\">Appointee lost election to finish the term.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-11\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />Successor <a href=\"/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_special_election_in_Ohio\" title=\"2026 United States Senate special election in Ohio\">elected</a> November 3, 2026, to finish the term ending January 3, 2029.\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"Brown, Sherrod\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sherrod_Brown\" title=\"Sherrod Brown\">Sherrod Brown</a></span></span></span><br />(D)\n</td>\n<td>December 15, 2026\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br /><span class=\"error mw-ext-cite-error\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Cite error: There are <code>&lt;ref&#160;group&#61;lower-alpha&gt;</code> tags&#160;or <code>&#123;&#123;efn&#125;&#125;</code> templates on this page, but the references will not show without a <code>&#123;&#123;reflist&#124;group&#61;lower-alpha&#125;&#125;</code> template&#160;or <code>&#123;&#123;notelist&#125;&#125;</code> template (see the <a href=\"/wiki/Help:Cite_errors/Cite_error_group_refs_without_references\" title=\"Help:Cite errors/Cite error group refs without references\">help page</a>).</span></p><div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1333433106\">.mw-parser-output cite.citation{font-style:inherit;word-wrap:break-word}.mw-parser-output .citation q{quotes:\"\\\"\"\"\\\"\"\"'\"\"'\"}.mw-parser-output .citation:target{background-color:rgba(0,127,255,0.133)}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-free.id-lock-free a{background:url(\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Lock-green.svg\")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-limited.id-lock-limited a,.m